{"_id":"6a2feefe2204ffbc59e5a2e8","roadmapSlug":"python-data-analysis","nodeId":"la9oiXURvw6AH-Vuh-WqT","description":"# List Comprehensions\n\nList comprehensions provide a concise syntax for creating lists by applying an expression to each item in an iterable, optionally filtering with a condition. For example: `[x**2 for x in range(10) if x % 2 == 0]`. They are faster and more readable than equivalent `for` loops for simple transformations.","resources":[{"type":"official","title":"List Comprehensions","url":"https://docs.python.org/3/tutorial/datastructures.html#list-comprehensions","_id":"6a75d326b0650226a50aeb56"},{"type":"article","title":"When to Use a List Comprehension in Python Quiz","url":"https://realpython.com/quizzes/list-comprehension-python/","_id":"6a75d326b0650226a50aeb57"},{"type":"article","title":"List Comprehensions in Python","url":"https://towardsdatascience.com/list-comprehensions-in-python-28d54c9286ca/","_id":"6a75d326b0650226a50aeb58"}],"createdAt":"2026-06-15T12:24:30.180Z","updatedAt":"2026-08-07T12:44:22.099Z","lessonPacks":[],"paidResources":[{"_id":"6a5e3360acf8c05faf5e1c2a","title":"DataCamp - Data Analyst with Python","partner":"DataCamp","type":"course","url":"https://datacamp.pxf.io/QY0dY9"},{"_id":"6a5e3365acf8c05faf5e1ded","title":"DataCamp - Python Data Fundamentals","partner":"DataCamp","type":"course","url":"https://datacamp.pxf.io/k4V24x"}],"contribution":"https://github.com/kamranahmedse/developer-roadmap/tree/master/roadmaps/python-data-analysis/content/la9oiXURvw6AH-Vuh-WqT.md"}